#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:19
msgid ""
"This example shows how to migrate an example C++ package from ROS 1 to ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:22
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:24
msgid ""
"You need a working ROS 2 installation, such as :doc:`ROS rolling <../../Get-"
"Started/Installation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:27
msgid "The ROS 1 code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:29
msgid ""
"Say you have a ROS 1 package called ``talker`` that uses ``roscpp`` in one "
"node, called ``talker``. This package is in a catkin workspace, located at "
"``~/ros1_talker``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:32
msgid "Your ROS 1 workspace has the following directory layout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:34
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros1_talker\n"
"$ find .\n"
".\n"
"./src\n"
"./src/talker\n"
"./src/talker/package.xml\n"
"./src/talker/CMakeLists.txt\n"
"./src/talker/talker.cpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:45
msgid "The files have the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:47
msgid "``src/talker/package.xml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:49
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n"
"<?xml-model href=\"http://download.ros.org/schema/package_format2.xsd\" "
"schematypens=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\"?>\n"
"<package format=\"2\">\n"
"  <name>talker</name>\n"
"  <version>0.0.0</version>\n"
"  <description>talker</description>\n"
"  <maintainer email=\"gerkey@example.com\">Brian Gerkey</maintainer>\n"
"  <license>Apache-2.0</license>\n"
"  <buildtool_depend>catkin</buildtool_depend>\n"
"  <depend>roscpp</depend>\n"
"  <depend>std_msgs</depend>\n"
"</package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:64
msgid "``src/talker/CMakeLists.txt``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:66
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8.3)\n"
"project(talker)\n"
"find_package(catkin REQUIRED COMPONENTS roscpp std_msgs)\n"
"catkin_package()\n"
"include_directories(${catkin_INCLUDE_DIRS})\n"
"add_executable(talker talker.cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(talker ${catkin_LIBRARIES})\n"
"install(TARGETS talker\n"
"  RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CATKIN_PACKAGE_BIN_DESTINATION})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:78
msgid "``src/talker/talker.cpp``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:80
msgid ""
"#include <sstream>\n"
"#include \"ros/ros.h\"\n"
"#include \"std_msgs/String.h\"\n"
"int main(int argc, char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"  ros::init(argc, argv, \"talker\");\n"
"  ros::NodeHandle n;\n"
"  ros::Publisher chatter_pub = n.advertise<std_msgs::String>(\"chatter\", "
"1000);\n"
"  ros::Rate loop_rate(10);\n"
"  int count = 0;\n"
"  std_msgs::String msg;\n"
"  while (ros::ok())\n"
"  {\n"
"    std::stringstream ss;\n"
"    ss << \"hello world \" << count++;\n"
"    msg.data = ss.str();\n"
"    ROS_INFO(\"%s\", msg.data.c_str());\n"
"    chatter_pub.publish(msg);\n"
"    ros::spinOnce();\n"
"    loop_rate.sleep();\n"
"  }\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:107
msgid "Migrating to ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:109
msgid "Let's start by creating a new workspace in which to work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:111
msgid ""
"$ mkdir ~/ros2_talker\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:116
msgid ""
"We'll copy the source tree from our ROS 1 package into that workspace, where "
"we can modify it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:118
msgid ""
"$ mkdir src\n"
"$ cp -a ~/ros1_talker/src/talker src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:123
msgid ""
"Now we'll modify the C++ code in the node. The ROS 2 C++ library, called "
"``rclcpp``, provides a different API from that provided by ``roscpp``. The "
"concepts are very similar between the two libraries, which makes the changes "
"reasonably straightforward to make."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:130
msgid "Included headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:132
msgid ""
"In place of ``ros/ros.h``, which gave us access to the ``roscpp`` library "
"API, we need to include ``rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp``, which gives us access to the "
"``rclcpp`` library API:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:136
msgid ""
"//#include \"ros/ros.h\"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:141
msgid ""
"To get the ``std_msgs/String`` message definition, in place of ``std_msgs/"
"String.h``, we need to include ``std_msgs/msg/string.hpp``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:144
msgid ""
"//#include \"std_msgs/String.h\"\n"
"#include \"std_msgs/msg/string.hpp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:150
msgid "Changing C++ library calls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:152
msgid ""
"Instead of passing the node's name to the library initialization call, we do "
"the initialization, then pass the node name to the creation of the node "
"object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:155
msgid ""
"//  ros::init(argc, argv, \"talker\");\n"
"//  ros::NodeHandle n;\n"
"    rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"    auto node = rclcpp::Node::make_shared(\"talker\");"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:162
msgid ""
"The creation of the publisher and rate objects looks pretty similar, with "
"some changes to the names of namespace and methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:165
msgid ""
"//  ros::Publisher chatter_pub = n.advertise<std_msgs::String>(\"chatter\", "
"1000);\n"
"//  ros::Rate loop_rate(10);\n"
"  auto chatter_pub = node->create_publisher<std_msgs::msg::"
"String>(\"chatter\",\n"
"    1000);\n"
"  rclcpp::Rate loop_rate(10);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:173
msgid ""
"To further control how message delivery is handled, a quality of service "
"(``QoS``) profile could be passed in. The default profile is "
"``rmw_qos_profile_default``. For more details, see the `design document "
"<https://design.ros2.org/articles/qos.html>`__ and :doc:`concept overview "
"<../../ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:180
msgid "The creation of the outgoing message is different in the namespace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:182
msgid ""
"//  std_msgs::String msg;\n"
"  std_msgs::msg::String msg;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:187
msgid "In place of ``ros::ok()``, we call ``rclcpp::ok()``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:189
msgid ""
"//  while (ros::ok())\n"
"  while (rclcpp::ok())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:194
msgid "Inside the publishing loop, we access the ``data`` field as before:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:196
msgid "msg.data = ss.str();"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:200
msgid ""
"To print a console message, instead of using ``ROS_INFO()``, we use "
"``RCLCPP_INFO()`` and its various cousins. The key difference is that "
"``RCLCPP_INFO()`` takes a Logger object as the first argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:205
msgid ""
"//    ROS_INFO(\"%s\", msg.data.c_str());\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(node->get_logger(), \"%s\\n\", msg.data.c_str());"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:210
msgid "Change the publish call to use the ``->`` operator instead of ``.``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:212
msgid ""
"//    chatter_pub.publish(msg);\n"
"    chatter_pub->publish(msg);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:217
msgid ""
"Spinning (i.e., letting the communications system process any pending "
"incoming/outgoing messages until no more work is available) is different in "
"that the call now takes the node and timeout as arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:221
msgid ""
"//    ros::spinOnce();\n"
"    rclcpp::spin_all(node, 0s);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:226
msgid "Sleeping using the rate object is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:228
msgid "Putting it all together, the new ``talker.cpp`` looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:230
msgid ""
"#include <chrono>\n"
"#include <sstream>\n"
"// #include \"ros/ros.h\"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\"\n"
"// #include \"std_msgs/String.h\"\n"
"#include \"std_msgs/msg/string.hpp\"\n"
"\n"
"using namespace std::chrono_literals;\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"//  ros::init(argc, argv, \"talker\");\n"
"//  ros::NodeHandle n;\n"
"  rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"  auto node = rclcpp::Node::make_shared(\"talker\");\n"
"//  ros::Publisher chatter_pub = n.advertise<std_msgs::String>(\"chatter\", "
"1000);\n"
"//  ros::Rate loop_rate(10);\n"
"  auto chatter_pub = node->create_publisher<std_msgs::msg::"
"String>(\"chatter\", 1000);\n"
"  rclcpp::Rate loop_rate(10);\n"
"  int count = 0;\n"
"//  std_msgs::String msg;\n"
"  std_msgs::msg::String msg;\n"
"//  while (ros::ok())\n"
"  while (rclcpp::ok())\n"
"  {\n"
"    std::stringstream ss;\n"
"    ss << \"hello world \" << count++;\n"
"    msg.data = ss.str();\n"
"//    ROS_INFO(\"%s\", msg.data.c_str());\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(node->get_logger(), \"%s\\n\", msg.data.c_str());\n"
"//    chatter_pub.publish(msg);\n"
"    chatter_pub->publish(msg);\n"
"//    ros::spinOnce();\n"
"    rclcpp::spin_all(node, 0s);\n"
"    loop_rate.sleep();\n"
"  }\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:272
msgid "Change the ``package.xml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:274
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages use CMake functions and macros from ``ament_cmake_ros`` "
"instead of ``catkin``. Delete the dependency on ``catkin``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:277
msgid ""
"<!-- delete this -->\n"
"<buildtool_depend>catkin</buildtool_depend>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:282
msgid "Add a new dependency on ``ament_cmake_ros``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:284
msgid "<buildtool_depend>ament_cmake_ros</buildtool_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:288
msgid ""
"ROS 2 C++ libraries use `rclcpp <https://index.ros.org/p/rclcpp/#rolling>`__ "
"instead of `roscpp <https://index.ros.org/p/roscpp/#noetic>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:290
msgid "Delete the dependency on ``roscpp``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:292
msgid ""
"<!-- delete this -->\n"
"<depend>roscpp</depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:297
msgid "Add a dependency on ``rclcpp``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:299
msgid "<depend>rclcpp</depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:304
msgid ""
"Add an ``<export>`` section to tell colcon the package is an ``ament_cmake`` "
"package instead of a ``catkin`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:306
msgid ""
"<export>\n"
"  <build_type>ament_cmake</build_type>\n"
"</export>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:312
msgid "Your ``package.xml`` now looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:314
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n"
"<?xml-model href=\"http://download.ros.org/schema/package_format2.xsd\" "
"schematypens=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\"?>\n"
"<package format=\"2\">\n"
"  <name>talker</name>\n"
"  <version>0.0.0</version>\n"
"  <description>talker</description>\n"
"  <maintainer email=\"gerkey@example.com\">Brian Gerkey</maintainer>\n"
"  <license>Apache-2.0</license>\n"
"  <buildtool_depend>ament_cmake</buildtool_depend>\n"
"  <depend>rclcpp</depend>\n"
"  <depend>std_msgs</depend>\n"
"  <export>\n"
"    <build_type>ament_cmake</build_type>\n"
"  </export>\n"
"</package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:334
msgid "Changing the CMake code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:336
msgid ""
"Require a newer version of CMake so that ``ament_cmake`` functions work "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:338
msgid "cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:342
msgid ""
"Use a newer C++ standard matching the version used by your target ROS distro "
"in `REP 2000 <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2000/>`__. If you are using "
"C++20, then set that version with the following snippet after the "
"``project(talker)`` call. Add extra compiler checks too because it is a good "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:346
msgid ""
"if(NOT CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD)\n"
"  set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)\n"
"endif()\n"
"if(CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES \"Clang\")\n"
"  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic)\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:355
msgid ""
"Replace the ``find_package(catkin ...)`` call with individual calls for each "
"dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:357
msgid ""
"find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(std_msgs REQUIRED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:363
msgid ""
"Delete the call to ``catkin_package()``. Add a call to ``ament_package()`` "
"at the bottom of the ``CMakeLists.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:366
msgid "ament_package()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:370
msgid ""
"Make the ``target_link_libraries`` call modern CMake targets provided by "
"``rclcpp`` and ``std_msgs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:372
msgid ""
"target_link_libraries(talker PUBLIC\n"
"  rclcpp::rclcpp\n"
"  std_msgs::std_msgs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:378
msgid ""
"Delete the call to ``include_directories()``. Add a call to "
"``target_include_directories()`` below ``add_executable(talker talker."
"cpp)``. Don't pass variables like ``rclcpp_INCLUDE_DIRS`` into "
"``target_include_directories()``. The include directories are already "
"handled by calling ``target_link_libraries()`` with modern CMake targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:383
msgid ""
"target_include_directories(talker PUBLIC\n"
"   \"$<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>\"\n"
"   \"$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include/${PROJECT_NAME}>\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:389
msgid ""
"Change the call to ``install()`` so that the ``talker`` executable is "
"installed into a project specific directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:391
msgid ""
"install(TARGETS talker\n"
"  DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:396
msgid "The new ``CMakeLists.txt`` looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-CPP-Package-Example.rst:398
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)\n"
"project(talker)\n"
"if(NOT CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD)\n"
"  set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)\n"
"endif()\n"
"if(CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES \"Clang\")\n"
"  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic)\n"
"endif()\n"
"find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(std_msgs REQUIRED)\n"
"add_executable(talker talker.cpp)\n"
"target_include_directories(talker PUBLIC\n"
"   \"$<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>\"\n"
"   \"$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include/${PROJECT_NAME}>\")\n"
"target_link_libraries(talker PUBLIC\n"
"  rclcpp::rclcpp\n"
"  std_msgs::std_msgs)\n"
"install(TARGETS talker\n"
"  DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME})\n"
"ament_package()"
msgstr ""

